      "x": 736,
      "y": 2089,
      "width": 584,
      "height": 81,
      "visible": true,
      "text": "Groups can’t pool rewards Friends may have significant rewards collectively, but few tools show what becomes possible when their points are considered together."
    },
    {
      "id": "90:27",
      "parent": "413:54",
      "type": "TEXT",
      "x": 736,
      "y": 1988,
      "width": 584,
      "height": 81,
      "visible": true,
      "text": "Finding the best redemption requires expertise Comparing cash, points, transfer partners, and booking portals means navigating different values, rules, and systems."
    },
    {
      "id": "90:26",
      "parent": "413:54",
      "type": "TEXT",
      "x": 736,
      "y": 1887,
      "width": 584,
      "height": 81,
      "visible": true,
      "text": "Scattered rewards Travelers accumulate points across credit cards, airlines, and hotels without a clear view of what they can unlock together."
    },
    {
      "id": "123:17",
      "parent": "413:54",
      "type": "TEXT",
      "x": 734,
      "y": 1789,
      "width": 586,
      "height": 78,
      "visible": true,
      "text": "Point.ly began as a startup concept from a United Airlines manager who wanted to give travelers one view of their rewards. Travelers face three problems:",
      "fontSize": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "90:20",
      "parent": "413:54",
      "type": "TEXT",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 1789,
      "width": 472,
      "height": 76,
      "visible": true,
      "text": "The  \nChallenge",
      "fontSize": 38
    },
